# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Several tests here assert that a GENERATED file is byte-identical to what its
# generator produces — `adapter-claude/src/registry.ts` against
# `surface/generate-registry.mjs`, and the sanitized captures against the
# sanitiser. Generators write `\n`. Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites
# those files to CRLF and the comparison fails on line endings rather than on
# content, which is both a false alarm and one that can never be fixed in the
# generator.
#
# No tracked file contains CRLF today, so this changes no content — it only
# stops git from introducing any.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shims are the one thing that genuinely needs CRLF: cmd.exe is
# unreliable with LF-only batch files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary fixtures must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.node binary
